// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 07-resource-authority
// facility: rule.value-object.write [Write-Resource-Overwrite-Rejected]; D-0049; D-0095; conf.overwrite-optional-field-dynamic
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.overwrite-of-live-resource (dynamic)
//
// D-0095 refutes statically only where every value of the field's type
// owns a resource. An `Option<String>` field may hold `None`, which owns
// nothing (assigning over it is fine), so whether this assignment loses
// a resource is the value's to decide: here it holds `Some`, and the
// write faults when it runs.

import std;

struct Holder
{
    Option<String> s;
}

fn main()
{
    Holder h = Holder { .s = None };
    h.s = Some(String::from_str("first"));
    h.s = Some(String::from_str("second"));
}
